This source milestone added working **`watch`**, **`fix`**, and **`ci`** command
paths. Generation can use an existing Istanbul coverage report to select files
below a statement threshold; it also reads project test conventions and tracks
source dependencies. Ollama remains the local default, with optional configured
cloud model providers.

Generated files need review. Normal generation, watch, and fix can replace
existing sibling tests. The `ci --coverage` check currently can pass if the
coverage report is missing, so its success is not proof of improved coverage.
This private source prototype has no verified public package or hosted access.

The older paired light/dark landing stills showed marketing claims, a waitlist,
and sample passing-test/coverage numbers, not recorded CLI output. They are
withdrawn from this entry.

## Current source-run CLI study · 2026-09-25

The paired transcript cards below render **actual Specwatch CLI output** from a
disposable TypeScript fixture, with local file paths shortened. A deterministic
loopback Responses-API stub supplied the model response: this was **not Ollama
or a real model**. The cards are designed evidence renders, not raw terminal
screenshots or a contemporaneous capture of the June milestone.

`gen --dry-run --no-validate` exited successfully and left an existing
hand-written test byte-identical. Normal `gen --no-validate` then replaced that
test; validation was skipped, so the run does not establish test quality. A
watched source edit triggered regeneration. Separately, `ci --coverage` exited
successfully with no coverage report, confirming the missing-report gate remains
open rather than proving any coverage improvement.

